  "description": "The dry reference riddim: a hollow, square-edged grunt that barks in tight eighth notes over a clean sine sub, with nothing hidden. Play: hold or stab F1, G1 and A#1 against a half-time kick at 140-150 BPM; the pulse snaps open and shut like a gate. Macros: Bark Depth widens the filter snap on every bark, Tone opens the top end, Grit pushes the hard clip and Chatter adds a sixteenth-note flutter.",
